Because one tradeoff on the execution client becomes either be

- (a) always able to respond immediately by some constant block (mempool access etc) maintenance so that `getPayload` could be fast even without prior warning;

- (b) only be able to return optimal blocks if given prior warning (but creating multiple flows, some of which would have to be supported but some of which would likely become seldom-used, creating a kind of dead code/calling surface in spec form);

or other options.
